// Routing eval fixtures for enrich. Check 5 (W2, v0.17).
// Each line: {intent, expected_skill, ambiguous_with?}.
// D-CX-6 rule: intent must paraphrase the trigger, not copy it.
// enrich is the CANONICAL entity (person/company) enrichment skill.
// Article enrichment is a DISTINCT skill (article-enrichment); intents
// here must describe person/company page work, not article dumps, so
// the two skills route to different use cases without ambiguity.
// Anchor on enrich-only triggers (create person page / update company
// page); avoid "look up" and "who is" which co-fire query, and avoid
// "enrich the article" family which co-fires article-enrichment.
{"intent": "create person page for this founder and fill in their background", "expected_skill": "enrich", "ambiguous_with": ["brain-ops"]}
{"intent": "update company page for them with the latest funding and team details", "expected_skill": "enrich", "ambiguous_with": ["brain-ops"]}
